# Performance

Optimize for fast loads on mobile — most visitors find the site via local search.

## Images

- Always use `next/image` — never raw `<img>` for content photos
- Provide `width`, `height`, and `sizes`; use `priority` only for above-the-fold hero
- Serve WebP/AVIF; compress portfolio images before adding to `public/`

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<Image src="/work/kitchen-1.jpg" alt="Kitchen remodel in Draper" width={800} height={600} sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw" />
```

## JavaScript & Rendering

- Server Components by default — minimize client JS
- Dynamic import heavy client components: `const Gallery = dynamic(() => import('./Gallery'))`
- No unnecessary `"use client"` — keeps bundles small
- Avoid large icon libraries; use `lucide-react` with named imports only

## Fonts & CSS

- Use `next/font` for web fonts — no `@import` from Google Fonts in CSS
- Tailwind utilities over custom CSS; purge unused styles automatically

## Data & Forms

- Static pages at build time; no client-side fetching for marketing content
- EmailJS loads only in the ContactForm client component
- Lazy-load below-the-fold carousels and galleries

## Targets

- Lighthouse Performance ≥ 90 on mobile
- LCP < 2.5s, CLS < 0.1, INP < 200ms
